{"id":"tyrosine","name":"Tyrosine","form":"capsule","status":"Well-documented","aliases":"","category":"Stimulant","chemicalClass":"Substituted phenethylamines, Amino acid","psychoactiveClass":"Stimulants","addictionPotential":"mildly habit forming","toxicity":["extremely low toxicity"],"summarySources":"PsychonautWiki","summary":"Tyrosine is a stimulant substance belonging to the Substituted phenethylamines, Amino acid chemical class.","doseMaxTick":5000,"doseUnit":"mg","doseRows":[{"roa":"Oral","source":"PsychonautWiki","unit":"mg","threshold":"300 mg","light":"500–1000 mg","common":"1000–2000 mg","strong":"2000–3000 mg","heavy":"3000 mg+","commonEstimate":1500,"band":{"low":1000,"high":2000},"domain":[240,4400],"segments":{"light":[500,1000],"common":[1000,2000],"strong":[2000,3000],"heavy":[3000,4224]}}],"durationSources":"PsychonautWiki","durationRows":[{"roa":"Oral","onset":"30–90 min","comeup":"—","peak":"1–3 h","offset":"—","afterEffects":"6–12 h","total":"2–4 h"}],"tolerance":{"buildUp":"after repeated and frequent usage","reset":"14 days","milestones":[{"label":"Full tolerance","value":"after repeated and frequent usage","tone":"danger"},{"label":"Half tolerance","value":"7 days","tone":"warning"},{"label":"Baseline","value":"14 days","tone":"positive"}],"crossTolerances":[{"group":"Cross-tolerance","items":["Dopamine"]}]},"subjectiveEffects":[],"combinations":[{"substance":"25x-NBOMe","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"25x-NBOH","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Tramadol","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MAOIs","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"DXM","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MDMA","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Stimulants","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Alcohol","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MXE","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Dissociatives","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."}],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and routes","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Tyrosine"}],"formula":"C9H11NO3","molarMass":181.19,"pharmacology":{"text":"The effects of tyrosine as a supplement or psychoactive compound are due to it being a precursor to catecholamine neurotransmitters. Supplemental L-Tyrosine is converted by the body into L-DOPA which is then decarboxylated into dopamine, which later turns into norepinephrine and is then finally converted to epinephrine. This means it effectively boosts the levels of these neurotransmitters in the brain, resulting in stimulating and euphoric effects.","source":"PsychonautWiki","page":"Tyrosine","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/Tyrosine#Pharmacology"},"uses":{"text":"L-Tyrosine or tyrosine (symbol Tyr or Y) or 4-hydroxyphenylalanine is one of the 20 standard amino acids that are used by cells to synthesize proteins.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Tyrosine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyrosine"}}